{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>El who brought him out of Egypt, etc.</b> The explanation follows the way of the Sages of blessed memory, that when Israel went out from Egypt they refined all the sparks of holiness that were in the shell of Egypt. And we have already introduced the principle that the power of holiness is manifested when it refines its offshoots, and this is what it says <b>who brought him out</b> etc. — <b>like the toafoth of a reem to him</b> — meaning, to the people. And therefore he also alluded to this in the statement <b>he shall eat the nations his adversaries</b>, for the eating is to extract the spark of holiness within them and have it absorbed into the soul of Israel, in the sod of (Proverbs 13:25) ״צַדִּיק אוֹכֵל לְשׂוֹבַע נַפְשׁוֹ״. And his saying <b>and their bones</b> means: even the aspect that strengthens itself within them, He will extract that too." "And his saying <b>and his arrows he shall strike</b> may be explained following the way of the Sages of blessed memory (Tanhuma, Beshalah 15) on the verse (Isaiah 24:21) ״יִפְקֹד ה׳ עַל צְבָא״ etc. — that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not destroy a nation below until He visits [punishment] upon its prince above. Now, when a nation is merely weakened, its prince above is not destroyed but HaShem humbles him; but when the nation suffers the fate of Sodom and Gomorrah, then its prince above is destroyed. And this is what it says <b>and his arrows</b> — meaning, the power of their array, which are the arrows that do battle on their behalf, namely the princes — <b>he shall strike</b>, following the usage of (Psalms 110:6) ״מָחַץ רֹאשׁ עַל אֶרֶץ רַבָּה״ — that the power of their princes above will be destroyed. And if we interpret ״יִמְחָץ״ in the sense of immersion and washing, the intent is to say that no arrow is flung that does not pierce them and become immersed in their blood."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:45.645837804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}